# Send one MOVE_JS frame: the streaming primitive the control stack uses (SDK
# Arm::move_js).
#
# This is a single frame, not a stream. The firmware's command watchdog trips 100 ms
# after the last frame, so one frame only holds that long -- continuous servo needs a
# caller that re-sends, which is what litearm_ros2_control's write() does. dq doubles
# as the slew limit of the position reference; with dq all zero the firmware freezes
# its own reference and refuses a target more than 5 mrad away. Leave tau_ff empty to
# keep the firmware's built-in feedforward, which supplying tau switches off.
# Refused unless allow_motion:=true.

float64[] q               # one reference per axis; empty is rejected by the SDK
float64[] dq              # empty means all zero
float64[] tau_ff          # empty means "let the firmware compute it"
---
bool success
string message
